    "text": "Hydrogen peroxide oxidises <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mi>to</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> in acidic medium, but reduces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mi>to</mi><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> in alkaline medium. The other products formed are, respectively",
